## ⚡ Can Your Backend Handle 100+ Orders/Day on Vercel?

### Short Answer: **YES, but barely — and reporting endpoints WILL be slow.**

### Detailed Assessment:

| Factor | Status | Details |
|--------|--------|---------|
| **Vercel Cold Starts** | ⚠️ Risky | Every serverless function has ~500ms-2s cold start. Your `connectDB()` middleware adds more latency |
| **Function Timeout** | ⚠️ 10s limit | Vercel free/hobby has 10s max execution. `getMonthlySalesSummary` with 3000+ orders **will timeout** |
| **Memory** | ⚠️ 1GB limit | Loading all orders into memory for reports will hit limits at ~5000-10000 orders |
| **MongoDB Connection** | ✅ Good | Your `global.mongoose` caching pattern is correct for serverless |
| **Connection Pool** | ⚠️ Risk | `maxPoolSize: 10` × concurrent functions = could hit Atlas connection limit |
| **Order Creation** | ✅ Fine | ~200-500ms per order (DB write + Pusher + optional Stripe) |
| **Order List** | ⚠️ No pagination | Will degrade as orders grow |
| **POS Menu Feed** | ✅ Excellent | In-memory cache works perfectly |
| **Real-time (Pusher)** | ✅ Fine | Fire-and-forget pattern is correct |

### Specific Numbers:

```
100 orders/day × 365 days = 36,500 orders/year

GET /api/orders (no pagination) → 36,500 documents loaded → ~5-10 seconds
GET /api/orders/monthly-sales-summary → 3,000 docs × JS processing → ~3-8 seconds
GET /api/orders/sales-summary → 100-500 docs → ~500ms-2s (OK for daily)
GET /api/orders/dashboard-metrics → 3,000 docs → ~2-5 seconds
```

> [!WARNING]
> **After 6 months (18,000+ orders), your reporting endpoints will start timing out on Vercel's 10-second limit.** The `getAllOrders` endpoint without pagination will also become unusable.

### Quick Fixes for 100/day on Vercel:

1. ✅ Add pagination to `getAllOrders` (limit 50 per page)
2. ✅ Convert `getSalesSummary` to aggregation pipeline
3. ✅ Convert `getMonthlySalesSummary` to aggregation pipeline
4. ✅ Add `.select()` projection where missing (e.g., getMonthlySalesSummary Line 1476 — `.lean()` without `.select()` fetches ENTIRE order document)

