## 🏗️ V2 Multi-Restaurant (50+ Branches) — What's Needed

### Current V1 Architecture Problem:

```
Single MongoDB database → Single collection per entity → No tenant isolation
```

All orders, products, expenses go into **one collection**. This works for 1 restaurant. For 50+ it's a disaster.

---

### Required Architecture Changes:

### 1. 🔑 Tenant ID (Restaurant/Branch ID) — MUST ADD TO EVERY MODEL

Every model needs a `branchId` or `restaurantId` field:

```javascript
// EVERY schema needs this:
const orderSchema = new mongoose.Schema({
  branchId: { 
    type: mongoose.Schema.Types.ObjectId, 
    ref: 'Branch',
    required: true,
    index: true  // CRITICAL for performance
  },
  // ... existing fields
});

// Compound indexes change to:
orderSchema.index({ branchId: 1, createdAt: -1 });
orderSchema.index({ branchId: 1, status: 1, createdAt: -1 });
```

**Models that need `branchId`**:
- Order ✅
- Product ✅
- Category ✅
- ModifierGroup ✅
- Expense ✅
- Deposit ✅
- Payment ✅
- Promo (could be global or per-branch) ✅
- OrderCounter ✅

### 2. 🏢 New Models Needed

```javascript
// Restaurant model (parent entity)
const restaurantSchema = {
  name: String,
  ownerEmail: String,
  plan: { type: String, enum: ['basic', 'pro', 'enterprise'] },
  settings: { taxRate, currency, timezone },
  createdAt: Date
};

// Branch model (child of restaurant)
const branchSchema = {
  restaurantId: ObjectId,
  name: String,
  address: String,
  phone: String,
  isActive: Boolean,
  settings: { /* branch-specific overrides */ }
};

// User model (for auth)
const userSchema = {
  email: String,
  passwordHash: String,
  role: { type: String, enum: ['super-admin', 'owner', 'manager', 'employee'] },
  restaurantId: ObjectId,  // which restaurant they belong to
  branchIds: [ObjectId],   // which branches they can access
  permissions: [String]
};
```

### 3. 🔐 Authentication & Authorization — MANDATORY

| Layer | Technology | Purpose |
|-------|-----------|---------|
| Auth tokens | JWT (jsonwebtoken) | User login/session |
| Password | bcrypt | Password hashing |
| Middleware | Custom auth middleware | Extract user + branchId from token |
| RBAC | Role-based access control | super-admin, owner, manager, employee |
| Rate limiting | express-rate-limit | Prevent abuse |
| Input validation | Joi / Zod | Validate req.body and query params |

### 4. 🔴 Redis — YES, You Need It

| Use Case | Why Redis | Priority |
|----------|-----------|----------|
| **POS Menu Cache** | Your current `cachedPOSMenuFeed` variable only works in a single process. On Vercel, each serverless function is a new process = cache miss every time | 🔴 HIGH |
| **Session Store** | JWT blacklisting, token refresh | 🔴 HIGH |
| **Rate Limiting** | Distributed rate limiting across serverless functions | 🟡 MEDIUM |
| **Real-time state** | Order status cache, kitchen display cache | 🟡 MEDIUM |
| **Dashboard Metrics Cache** | Cache computed dashboard results for 5 minutes | 🟢 NICE |

**Recommended**: [Upstash Redis](https://upstash.com/) — serverless-friendly, pay-per-request, perfect for Vercel.

```javascript
// Example: POS Menu cache with Redis
const Redis = require('@upstash/redis');
const redis = new Redis({ url: process.env.UPSTASH_REDIS_URL, token: process.env.UPSTASH_REDIS_TOKEN });

exports.getPOSMenuFeed = async (branchId) => {
  const cacheKey = `pos-menu:${branchId}`;
  const cached = await redis.get(cacheKey);
  if (cached) return cached;

  const feed = await buildMenuFeed(branchId);
  await redis.set(cacheKey, JSON.stringify(feed), { ex: 300 }); // 5 min TTL
  return feed;
};
```

### 5. 🟡 BullMQ — YES, For Background Jobs

| Job | Why BullMQ | Current Problem |
|-----|-----------|-----------------|
| **PDF Generation** | Receipt & report PDFs are generated synchronously during request. For 50 branches generating reports = timeout | Blocks response |
| **Email Notifications** | Order confirmation emails (nodemailer is installed but unused) | Not implemented |
| **Daily Report Aggregation** | Pre-compute daily summaries at midnight instead of on-demand | Slow queries |
| **Promo Usage Tracking** | Async increment without blocking order creation | Minor delay acceptable |
| **Cloudinary Cleanup** | Batch delete unused images | Manual currently |

**But...** BullMQ needs a persistent Redis connection and a worker process. **This doesn't work on Vercel serverless.**

> [!IMPORTANT]
> ### For V2, you need to move off Vercel to one of these:
> | Option | Cost | Complexity | Recommendation |
> |--------|------|-----------|----------------|
> | **Railway.app** | $5-20/mo | Low | ✅ Best for your stage |
> | **Render.com** | $7-25/mo | Low | ✅ Good alternative |
> | **DigitalOcean App Platform** | $12-24/mo | Medium | ✅ Good for growth |
> | **AWS ECS / EC2** | $20-50/mo | High | For later scale |
> | **Vercel + Inngest/Trigger.dev** | $10-30/mo | Medium | If staying on Vercel |

### 6. 📊 Database Strategy for 50+ Branches

| Approach | Pros | Cons | Recommended? |
|----------|------|------|-------------|
| **Shared DB + branchId field** | Simple, low cost | All data in one collection | ✅ For up to 50 branches |
| **Separate DB per restaurant** | Full isolation | Complex connection management | ❌ Overkill for now |
| **Sharded cluster** | Unlimited scale | Expensive, complex | ❌ Way too early |

**Recommendation**: **Shared DB with `branchId`** on every document + compound indexes. This handles 50+ branches with up to 100K+ orders easily.

### 7. 📝 Additional V2 Features Checklist

| Feature | New Tech Needed | Priority |
|---------|----------------|----------|
| Authentication (JWT) | jsonwebtoken, bcrypt | 🔴 MUST |
| Input validation | Joi or Zod | 🔴 MUST |
| Rate limiting | express-rate-limit + Redis | 🔴 MUST |
| Pagination on all list endpoints | Built-in | 🔴 MUST |
| API versioning (/api/v2/) | Express router | 🟡 HIGH |
| Request/response compression | compression middleware | 🟡 HIGH |
| Health check with DB ping | Mongoose readyState | 🟢 LOW |
| Webhook for Stripe events | Stripe webhook handler | 🔴 MUST |
| Audit log (who changed what) | New AuditLog model | 🟡 HIGH |
| Soft deletes (instead of hard delete) | isDeleted flag | 🟡 HIGH |
| Image optimization | Cloudinary transforms | 🟢 LOW |
| API documentation | Swagger/OpenAPI | 🟡 HIGH |
