## 🔧 Other Code Issues Found

### 1. `connectDB()` Called Twice
In [app.js](file:///c:/Users/yoges/Desktop/Cyber%20Nest/restaurant-management-system/backend/src/app.js) Line 15 and Line 18-29:
```javascript
connectDB();  // Line 15 — called on module load

app.use(async (req, res, next) => {  // Line 18 — called on EVERY request
  await connectDB();
  next();
});
```
The middleware version is correct for Vercel serverless. **Remove Line 15** — it's redundant and adds a cold-start DB call.

### 2. ProductId Generation — Full Table Scan
In [product.model.js](file:///c:/Users/yoges/Desktop/Cyber%20Nest/restaurant-management-system/backend/src/modules/menu/models/product.model.js) Lines 60-75:
```javascript
const products = await Product.find({ productId: { $regex: /^M\d+$/ } }, 'productId');
```
**This scans ALL products** on every new product creation. Should use an auto-incrementing counter like OrderCounter.

### 3. POS Menu Cache Never Expires
In [menu.service.js](file:///c:/Users/yoges/Desktop/Cyber%20Nest/restaurant-management-system/backend/src/modules/menu/services/menu.service.js) Line 7:
```javascript
let cachedPOSMenuFeed = null;  // Never expires, only cleared on writes
```
On Vercel, this variable resets on every cold start anyway, so the cache is essentially useless in production. Add Redis or TTL-based caching.

### 4. Stripe Initialized Even if Key is Missing
In [order.service.js](file:///c:/Users/yoges/Desktop/Cyber%20Nest/restaurant-management-system/backend/src/modules/order/services/order.service.js) Line 7:
```javascript
const stripe = require("stripe")(process.env.STRIPE_SECRET_KEY || "sk_test_mock");
```
This creates a Stripe instance with a fake key, which will throw misleading errors.

### 5. `markOrderPaid` Saves Payments One-by-One
[order.service.js](file:///c:/Users/yoges/Desktop/Cyber%20Nest/restaurant-management-system/backend/src/modules/order/services/order.service.js) Lines 257-268:
```javascript
for (const p of payments) {
  const paymentDoc = new Payment({...});
  await paymentDoc.save();  // Sequential writes!
}
```
Should use `Payment.insertMany(paymentDocs)` for batch insert.

### 6. `deleteModifierGroup` Has a Bug
[menu.service.js](file:///c:/Users/yoges/Desktop/Cyber%20Nest/restaurant-management-system/backend/src/modules/menu/services/menu.service.js) Line 105:
```javascript
const group = await ModifierGroup.deleteModifierGroup || await ModifierGroup.findByIdAndDelete(id);
```
`ModifierGroup.deleteModifierGroup` is **undefined** (it's not a Mongoose method). This line evaluates the OR and falls through to `findByIdAndDelete`, but it's a bug waiting to cause confusion.

