> **Bottom Line**: Your V1 backend architecture is **clean and well-structured** (modular design, service layer, proper error handling, Winston logging). But it's a **prototype-level** backend — no auth, no pagination, no query optimization for reporting. It works fine for a single restaurant with <100 orders/day today, but will start breaking at 6-12 months of data. For V2 multi-restaurant, you need fundamental changes — tenant isolation, auth, Redis, and likely moving off Vercel.
